+// b2373 BSA (Aggression spec_bsa_1113, owner: bush sneak attacks that know where their wards are). Runtime data flag, read first; 0 = v887.
+// Bit 1 PERCH IN RANGE: a ranged body in range of its focus may step onto an adjacent free bush tile from which the focus stays in my range
+// (bush_perch_step's candidates; live wants a strictly closer tile and runs only out of range); not when I kill the focus from here and
+// only when the focus came toward me or stood last round (the step costs the shot, GR:118). Bit 2 ENEMY WARD MEMORY: each body keeps the
+// foe wards it has seen, one per owner (RC X873 FWI1: wards are permanent, one per champion; no TTL), read every
+// BSA_POLL rounds, dropped when the tile is seen empty; bush_watched counts a remembered bush ward whose vision holds the tile as watching. Bit 4: not built (Step 0 names the mover first).
+#define BSA_BITS 0
+#define BSA_POLL 3 // bit 2: the ward records are read every this many rounds
+inline const volatile int BSA_TAB[3] = { 0x42534131, BSA_BITS, BSA_POLL }; // slot 0 magic keeps it out of .bss
+#define BSA_ON(b) ((BSA_TAB[1] & (b)) != 0)
